# SUPERSEDED, kept as a regression fixture. Do not build on this encoding.
#
# This is how assortative mating was encoded before co-paths existed (tasks 151346/151347):
# the covariances that assortment *induces* among the partners' causes were written out by hand
# as bidirected edges. That is legitimate only because g and e are roots here, and it is why the
# validation against relative_covariance.tex passed. It has two problems, both of which are why
# task-20260804-173343 introduced the co-path:
#
# 1. IT IS INCOMPLETE. Cov[e_m, e_p] is missing, so this model gives
#        Cov[y_m, y_p] = V_A_eq*rho_g + 2*V_E*rho_g
#    where the mating model requires rho_y*V_P. The shortfall is exactly rho_y*V_E^2/V_P -- the
#    absent term. At V_A_eq=0.46, V_E=0.6, rho_y=0.3: 0.2161 against the correct 0.3180.
#    The three terms that WERE written are the ones the lineal/collateral asymmetry needs, which
#    is why the omission never surfaced in the earlier validation.
#
# 2. IT DOES NOT SURVIVE A SECOND GENERATION. A gen-1 individual's g and e are endogenous, so a
#    bidirected edge between mates is a correlated *residual* and never reaches their ancestors.
#    Assortment induces correlation among ALL the causes of the matched variables, propagating
#    backward up the graph, which an S entry cannot do. At the allele level it would need
#    O(M^2) hand-derived entries per couple.
#
# tests/test_copath.py asserts that the co-path encoding in am_equilibrium.pmg reproduces every
# quantity this file gets right, and fixes the one it gets wrong.

units: unstandardized
latent: g_m, e_m, g_p, e_p, g_o1, e_o1, s_o1, g_o2, e_o2, s_o2
positive: V_A_eq, V_E, V_K, V_A0

label: g_m = $g_{m}$
label: e_m = $e_{m}$
label: y_m = $y_{m}$
label: g_p = $g_{p}$
label: e_p = $e_{p}$
label: y_p = $y_{p}$
label: g_o1 = $g_{o1}$
label: e_o1 = $e_{o1}$
label: y_o1 = $y_{o1}$
label: s_o1 = $s_{o1}$
label: g_o2 = $g_{o2}$
label: e_o2 = $e_{o2}$
label: y_o2 = $y_{o2}$
label: s_o2 = $s_{o2}$

y_m  ~ g_m  + e_m
y_p  ~ g_p  + e_p
y_o1 ~ g_o1 + e_o1
y_o2 ~ g_o2 + e_o2

g_o1 ~ 1/2*g_m + 1/2*g_p + s_o1
g_o2 ~ 1/2*g_m + 1/2*g_p + s_o2

g_m ~~ V_A_eq*g_m
g_p ~~ V_A_eq*g_p
g_m ~~ (rho_g*V_A_eq)*g_p

e_m  ~~ V_E*e_m
e_p  ~~ V_E*e_p
e_o1 ~~ V_E*e_o1
e_o2 ~~ V_E*e_o2
s_o1 ~~ V_K*s_o1
s_o2 ~~ V_K*s_o2

# each parent's environment correlated with the OTHER parent's genes -- but NOT e with e,
# which is the omission described above
e_m ~~ (rho_g*V_E)*g_p
e_p ~~ (rho_g*V_E)*g_m

assume: rho_g = rho_y*h2_eq
assume: h2_eq = V_A_eq/(V_A_eq + V_E)
assume: V_A_eq = V_A0/(1 - rho_g)
assume: V_K = V_A0/2
